3 CITY Gilbert
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kvinnherad Gards- og ættesoga 2 page 479 Ænes (32f), Slektsbok for Kvinnherad 1 page 470 Ænes (32f), Kvinnherad Gards- og ættesoga 3 page 670 Myklebust (88).
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob var husmann med jord på Træet under Myklebust i Uskedalen, Kvinnherad før de reiste til Amerika. Se Kvinnherad bygdebok bind 3, side 670 bruk 12 og 16 nr. 88. Ved folketellingen i 1880 bodde niesen Jacobine Enes hos dem i La
2 CONC fayette, Story Co., Iowa, oppgitt alder 15 år. (Oppgitt av Helge Bjørgen).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/113105809/jacob-thomasen
2 CONT
2 CONT His son, Thomas Jacobson Eness, who was first in the family of 5 boys and 2 girls to emigrate from Norway, brought his father over when he had a good farm in Gilbert.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Jacob died he was buried in Born Cemetery. When South Saint Petri Cemetery was established, the family moved Jacob and his stone there. That stone was badly worn so they had a new stone made and placed also. The dates on the 
2 CONC two stones are inexplicably off by a few days.
2 CONT
2 CONT [From What's Next...?: The Memoir of a Norwegian Iowan," July 4, 2013, by Paul Gene Eness, his great-great-grandson, page 8-9.Contributed by pMcP.] ]
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT Date of birth calculated from date of death at age 75 years 7 months 25 days. This is the same person as Jacob Thompson whose marker adjoins, with similar dates.
