2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/244184291/ole-oleson
2 CONT
2 CONT The Paxton Record (Paxton, IL)
2 CONT Thursday, Jan. 18, 1923
2 CONT
2 CONT OLE OLESON
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole Oleson Landa was born at Kjarland [Kjerland], Oskedale, Norway, the 6th day of March, in the year of 1842. On Sunday morning at 6:40, Jan. 14, he departed from this life, after an illness of seven weeks at the home of his daug
2 CONC hter, Mrs. Lewis Charleson, at Elliott, Ill.
2 CONT
2 CONT His age at the time of his death was 80 years, 10 months and 8 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Oleson was preceded in death by his wife, who died July 14, 1903, and son, James, who died May 3, 1914.
2 CONT
2 CONT Those left to mourn his death are two daughters and two sons, Mrs. Henry Nelson, of Gibson City; Mrs. Lewis Charleson, of Elliott; Mr. Orin Oleson, of Gibson City; Mr. Ole Oleson, in Norway, and nineteen grandchildren, one great g
2 CONC randson and hosts of friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services took place Tuesday, Rev. J. A. Carlson officiating. The body was laid to rest at the Pontippidan Cemetery.
